 you and your team have put into  getting us to this point  in my time as mayor it's probably the  the rate setting long-term plan process  that has been  one of the most challenging and it's  been back and forth back and forth  a number of times and to get it to the  point we are now  i find is really pleasing from from your  perspective  and also from as and while  it is 5.42 6.42 is  above where we had predicted it uh it is  certainly  quite a bit lower than the 8.22  that we were looking at uh two or three  weeks ago  so so thank you for that  mr chief executive do you want to make  any comment before we open that to  counsellors yeah thank you worship i  just  endorsed your comments and the uh  lornae's comments that she's eloquently  put forward to you about the final  result  i think it needs to be put in  perspective too that  you can't underestimate the effect that  the floods followed by  covert 19 and the lockdown took in terms  of our planning time  that really did erode into it and so we  were always  uh on the back foot a little bit that  coupled with  and laurene's introduction to the  organization in june  and then you have the very exacting  audit process that was used this year  has certainly ramped up the time  required  to actually deliver a completed plan  so we'll certainly reflect on that when  we um have our  usual post-mortem review but i think  the council can be satisfied that when  you  calculate both the proposed rate  increase this year  uh on top of the 2.84  of last year you are still under  comfortably  under the 10 threshold you've set  by 5 caps year on year  so given the the environment we're  working within  um i would submit to you that's a pretty  comforting place to be uh given that  we had some fairly stiff challenges  facing us over the last few months  so all in all we worship lessons to be  learned  relieved that we've now got to this  point as paul mccartney saying it's a  long unwinding road that leads us to  your door  